   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# FrugalProver — budget labeling with a local open model\n",
    "\n",
    "Runs the oracle pipeline's first two stages end to end:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Stage 1 `sample`** — draw a balanced problem set from MATH.\n",
    "2. **Stage 2 `budget`** — label each problem with the solve effort it needs, by\n",
    "   running the **solving agent** (`agent/` — prover → verifier → corrector) once\n",
    "   per token budget and recording the smallest budget that clears the success\n",
    "   threshold (`b_star`).\n",
    "\n",
    "The agent generates locally through `agent/model.py:HFClient` — no server, no\n",
    "inference-time network. `configs/agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml` runs the verify-repair loop on\n",
    "`DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B`; a CUDA GPU is used when present (bf16/fp16),\n",
    "otherwise it falls back to CPU. Same-model roles share **one** loaded copy.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Memory:** the 7B verify-repair loop wants a roomy GPU (A100/L4). On a smaller\n",
    "> card, edit the `model:` in `configs/agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml` to a lighter checkpoint\n",
    "> (e.g. `Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct`) — since same-model roles share one copy,\n",
    "> changing it in one place shrinks the whole loop."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install (GPU extra pulls torch + transformers)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clone the repo (or run from an existing checkout) and install the GPU extra,\n",
    "# which pulls torch + transformers (the base install is deliberately torch-free).\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/<your-org>/smiles-frugalprover.git\n",
    "%cd smiles-frugalprover\n",
    "!git checkout \"agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B\"\n",
    "!pip install -q -e \".[gpu]\""
   ]
   "source": "# Clone the repo (or run from an existing checkout) and install the GPU extra,\n# which pulls torch + transformers (the base install is deliberately torch-free).\n# [quant] adds bitsandbytes for `quantization: 4bit|8bit` -- CUDA-only wheels, so\n# drop it to \".[gpu]\" if you're staying at full precision.\n!git clone https://github.com/<your-org>/smiles-frugalprover.git\n%cd smiles-frugalprover\n!git checkout \"agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B\"\n!pip install -q -e \".[gpu,quant]\""
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Confirm the GPU is visible and the package imports without a torch hoist.\n",
    "!frugalprover info"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Stage 1 — sample problems from MATH\n",
    "\n",
    "`frugalprover sample` draws a balanced set and writes `data/<run>/problems.jsonl`\n",
    "(A1 records). Shrunk here to a handful for a quick demo; drop the `--set`\n",
    "overrides for the full balanced draw. All later stages resolve files inside the\n",
    "same run dir, so keep `--run-name` consistent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!frugalprover sample -c configs/base.yaml --run-name DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B \\\n",
    "  --set \"sample.subjects=[algebra, number_theory]\" \\\n",
    "  --set sample.per_level_per_subject=2 \\\n",
    "  --set sample.n_problems=6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Stage 2 — generate budgets with the agent\n",
    "\n",
    "`frugalprover budget` (estimator `sweep`, the default) runs the\n",
    "`DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml` agent once per budget in `budget.budgets`,\n",
    "grades the completions against the gold answer, and writes\n",
    "`data/<run>/budgets.jsonl` (A2).\n",
    "\n",
    "The budgets come from the agent config (`[8192, 16384, 32768]`) — sized to a\n",
    "reasoning-model verify-repair loop, where a single solve is already thousands of\n",
    "tokens. Each role's per-call cap is clamped to the budget, and the loop stops\n",
    "adding rounds once an attempt's running total reaches it (checked at round\n",
    "boundaries). Only `n_samples` is trimmed here to keep the demo cheaper.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a heavy run (a 7B loop generating tens of thousands of tokens per\n",
    "problem). It's **resumable** — rerun after a disconnect and it labels only\n",
    "what's missing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Uses the budgets from the agent config ([8192, 16384, 32768]); only trims\n",
    "# n_samples to keep the demo cheaper. Add --set \"budget.budgets=[...]\" to change\n",
    "# the sweep, but keep entries >= the prover's per-call cap (8192) so B buys\n",
    "# critique-repair rounds instead of just truncating one attempt.\n",
    "!frugalprover budget -c configs/base.yaml -c configs/agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml --run-name DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B \\\n",
    "  --set budget.n_samples=2"
   ]
   "source": "# Uses the budgets from the agent config ([8192, 16384, 32768]); only trims\n# n_samples to keep the demo cheaper. Add --set \"budget.budgets=[...]\" to change\n# the sweep, but keep entries >= the prover's per-call cap (8192) so B buys\n# critique-repair rounds instead of just truncating one attempt.\n#\n# On a 16GB card, uncomment the line below first: it flips all three roles to\n# 4bit at once (~5GB of weights instead of ~15GB). Do all three or none -- the\n# weight cache keys on (model, quantization), so a mismatch loads two copies and\n# leaves you worse off. `--set` can't index into agent.verifiers, hence the sed.\n# !sed -i 's/quantization: none/quantization: 4bit/' configs/agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml\n\n!frugalprover budget -c configs/base.yaml -c configs/agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml --run-name DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B \\\n  --set budget.n_samples=2"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Inspect the budget labels\n",
    "\n",
    "`b_star` is the smallest budget that cleared the threshold (`null` = censored,\n",
    "not solved within any budget). `p` is the success rate per budget, `sc` the\n",
    "self-consistency (plurality-vote) baseline, `tokens_spent` the total the agent\n",
    "actually generated across the sweep."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from frugalprover.common.config import load_config\n",
    "from frugalprover.common.io import read_jsonl\n",
    "\n",
    "cfg = load_config([\"configs/base.yaml\", \"configs/agent/DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml\"], overrides=[\"run_name=DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B\"])\n",
    "for row in read_jsonl(cfg.data_path(\"budgets.jsonl\")):\n",
    "    print(f\"[{row['id']}] b_star={row['b_star']} p={row['p']} \"\n",
    "          f\"sc={row['sc']} tokens_spent={row['tokens_spent']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Full trace — watch the agent solve one problem step by step\n",
    "\n",
    "The budget labels above are a summary (`b_star`, `p`, `tokens_spent`) — they\n",
    "don't show *how* the loop got there. This cell drives the same building blocks\n",
    "`VerifyRepairAgent` uses internally (`Prover`, `Verifier`, `Corrector`,\n",
    "`aggregate`, `collect_flaws` from `agent/roles.py` and `agent/aggregation.py`),\n",
    "but for a single problem, one attempt at a time, printing every round instead\n",
    "of batching silently. You'll see:\n",
    "\n",
    "- the prover's initial candidate,\n",
    "- each verifier's verdict and diagnosed flaws,\n",
    "- the corrector's repair (if the ensemble didn't accept), repeated up to\n",
    "  `agent.max_rounds`,\n",
    "- the final candidate graded against the gold answer, and the total tokens\n",
    "  spent across every call in the loop.\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses the first problem from `data/<run>/problems.jsonl` sampled in step 2."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "import textwrap\n\nfrom frugalprover.agent.aggregation import aggregate, collect_flaws\nfrom frugalprover.agent.model import build_model_client\nfrom frugalprover.agent.roles import Corrector, Prover, Verifier\nfrom frugalprover.common.grading import grade\nfrom frugalprover.common.records import ProblemRecord\n\n\ndef _show(label: str, text: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"--- {label} ---\")\n    print(textwrap.shorten(text, width=2000, placeholder=\" [...]\"))\n    print()\n\n\nproblem = ProblemRecord.from_dict(next(read_jsonl(cfg.data_path(\"problems.jsonl\"))))\nprint(f\"Problem [{problem.id}]: {problem.problem}\\nGold answer: {problem.answer}\\n\")\n\na = cfg.agent\nprover = Prover(build_model_client(a.prover), a.prover, a.prover_prompt, \"prover\")\ncorrector = Corrector(build_model_client(a.corrector), a.corrector, a.corrector_prompt, \"corrector\")\nverifiers = [Verifier(build_model_client(v), v, a.verifier_prompt, \"verifier\") for v in a.verifiers]\nfor role in [prover, corrector, *verifiers]:\n    role.client.setup()\n\ntry:\n    candidate = prover.propose([problem.problem])[0]\n    tokens = prover.count_tokens(candidate)\n    _show(\"round 0 -- prover proposes\", candidate)\n\n    accepted = False\n    for round_i in range(a.max_rounds):\n        critiques = [v.audit([(problem.problem, candidate)])[0] for v in verifiers]\n        tokens += sum(v.count_tokens(c.raw) for v, c in zip(verifiers, critiques))\n        for i, c in enumerate(critiques):\n            _show(f\"round {round_i + 1} -- verifier {i} ({'ACCEPT' if c.accept else 'REJECT'})\",\n                  c.raw or \"(empty response)\")\n\n        if aggregate(critiques, a.aggregation):\n            accepted = True\n            print(f\"Converged after round {round_i + 1} ({a.aggregation} rule).\\n\")\n            break\n\n        flaws = collect_flaws(critiques)\n        candidate = corrector.repair([(problem.problem, candidate, flaws)])[0]\n        tokens += corrector.count_tokens(candidate)\n        _show(f\"round {round_i + 1} -- corrector repairs\", candidate)\n    else:\n        status = \"flagged\" if a.on_nonconvergence == \"flag\" else \"rejected\"\n        print(f\"Hit max_rounds={a.max_rounds} without converging -> {status}.\\n\")\n\n    correct = grade(candidate, problem.answer)\n    print(f\"Final candidate {'PASSES' if correct else 'FAILS'} grading against the gold answer \"\n          f\"(accepted={accepted}); total tokens spent: {tokens}\")\nfinally:\n    for role in [prover, corrector, *verifiers]:\n        role.client.teardown()",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 6. (Optional) drive `HFClient` directly\n\n`HFClient` is a thin text-in / text-out interface — handy for a quick sanity\ncheck outside the pipeline. Point `model` at whatever `DeepSeek_R1_Distill_Qwen_7B.yaml` uses."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from frugalprover.agent.model import build_model_client\n",
    "from frugalprover.common.config import ModelSpec\n",
    "\n",
    "client = build_model_client(ModelSpec(client=\"hf\", model=\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\"))\n",
    "client.setup()\n",
    "out = client.generate(\n",
    "    [\"Problem: Compute 17 * 23. Give the answer in \\\\boxed{}.\"],\n",
    "    max_tokens=512, temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, role=\"prover\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(out[0])\n",
    "client.teardown()"
   ]
  }
